+/-!
+# Stock: the role-gated entry points succeed only on the registry's role answer
+
+Plain statement (one theorem per entry point): for every state, environment, caller and registry
+code, if a run of Stock's deployed bytes with the entry point's selector succeeds, then a static
+call to the registry with calldata `hasRole(ROLE, caller)` over the frame's starting persistent
+state succeeds with at least 32 bytes whose first word is `1`.  `ROLE` is the entry point's role
+constant, tied to its name by `keccak256` in Lean (`*_eq_keccak`).
+
+| entry point | selector | role |
+|---|---|---|
+| `pause()` | `0x8456cb59` | `TOKEN_PAUSER_ROLE` (`Pause.lean`) |
+| `unpause()` | `0x3f4ba83a` | `TOKEN_PAUSER_ROLE` |
+| `mint(address,uint256)` | `0x40c10f19` | `MINTER_ROLE` |
+| `burn(address,uint256)` | `0x9dc29fac` | `BURNER_ROLE` |
+| `adminBurn(address,uint256)` | `0x06dd0419` | `ADMIN_BURNER_ROLE` |
+| `pauseOracle()` | `0x253ea980` | `ORACLE_PAUSER_ROLE` |
+| `unpauseOracle()` | `0x0fab6865` | `ORACLE_PAUSER_ROLE` |
+| `setMetadata(string,string)` | `0x51335b50` | `METADATA_UPDATER_ROLE` |
+
+Premises, as for `pause_requires_role`: the frame starts at pc 0 of the registered runtime with an
+empty stack and memory, on a covered fork.  Each of these entry points asks for its role before
+anything else (after the ABI decoding of its arguments, which writes no memory), so the query is
+the frame's first external call and its world is the frame's own.
+
+The walk: the dispatcher route to the entry point's wrapper (`root_selected` and the selector
+comparisons), then `stock_walk` follows the wrapper, the argument decoder and the function body up
+to its call into `_checkRole(role)` (entry 88); `role_answered` takes it from there into entry
+119 and its `hasRole` query (`query_answered`).
+-/
+
